NAME
    gcloud alpha fault-testing experiment-templates delete - delete an
        experiment template

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha fault-testing experiment-templates delete
        (EXPERIMENT_TEMPLATE : --location=LOCATION) [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Delete an experiment template.

EXAMPLES
    To delete an experiment template test-template-id in location asia-east1
    run

        $ gcloud alpha fault-testing experiment-templates delete \
            test-template-id --location=asia-east1

POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
     ExperimentTemplate resource - The resource name of the experiment template
     to delete. Format:
     projects/{projectId}/locations/{location}/experimentTemplates/{experimentTemplateId}.
     The arguments in this group can be used to specify the attributes of this
     resource. (NOTE) Some attributes are not given arguments in this group but
     can be set in other ways.

     To set the project attribute:
      ◆ provide the argument experiment_template on the command line with a
        fully specified name;
      ◆ provide the argument --project on the command line;
      ◆ set the property core/project.

     This must be specified.

       EXPERIMENT_TEMPLATE
          ID of the experimentTemplate or fully qualified identifier for the
          experimentTemplate.

          To set the experiment_template attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument experiment_template on the command line.

          This positional argument must be specified if any of the other
          arguments in this group are specified.

       --location=LOCATION
          The location id of the experimentTemplate resource.

          To set the location attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument experiment_template on the command line with
            a fully specified name;
          ▸ provide the argument --location on the command line.

